\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Replication on three real communication graphs. (a)~On Enron the case-study hierarchy is reproduced (1-hop $<$ hand-crafted context $<$ temporal GNN) and the time shuffle levels the temporal detector to the hand-crafted result, so the advantage is causally temporal on a real topology. (b)~On two SNAP graphs the regime transition replicates: the volume detector wins the naive blast and collapses under the stealthy attacker, while the temporal detector holds.}}{12}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:realgraphs}{{6}{12}{Replication on three real communication graphs. (a)~On Enron the case-study hierarchy is reproduced (1-hop $<$ hand-crafted context $<$ temporal GNN) and the time shuffle levels the temporal detector to the hand-crafted result, so the advantage is causally temporal on a real topology. (b)~On two SNAP graphs the regime transition replicates: the volume detector wins the naive blast and collapses under the stealthy attacker, while the temporal detector holds}{table.6}{}}
