\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Base-rate arithmetic for the temporal GNN operating point (sensitivity $0.14$, FPR$1\%$): at a realistic prevalence of $1{:}10^4$ each detected attack comes with $\sim \!700$ false alarms, three orders of magnitude above the deployment threshold, which is why the detectors are triage instruments. ``FP per detected attack'' is $\alpha (1-\pi )/(r\pi )$, where $r$ is sensitivity, $\alpha $ is FPR, and $\pi $ is prevalence.}}{13}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:baserate}{{7}{13}{Base-rate arithmetic for the temporal GNN operating point (sensitivity $0.14$, FPR$1\%$): at a realistic prevalence of $1{:}10^4$ each detected attack comes with $\sim \!700$ false alarms, three orders of magnitude above the deployment threshold, which is why the detectors are triage instruments. ``FP per detected attack'' is $\alpha (1-\pi )/(r\pi )$, where $r$ is sensitivity, $\alpha $ is FPR, and $\pi $ is prevalence}{table.7}{}}
